  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =36-12 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=12$, $d=24$, and ${S}_{N}=588$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(12)+(N-1)(24)) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24+24N-24) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24N) \\\\ 588 & =12{N}^{2} \\\\ 49 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
